From: GLM-EXL3-2x-GB10 testing line <tensorfold-zig-testing@local>
Subject: glm-cuda: the follower's step in one broadcast, a window's greedy picks in one gather (Mia 1104 0031+0032, adapted to v1.2.3 + the adopted stack)

PROVENANCE: ported from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-DGX-Sparks-1104,
patches/engine/0031 (the follower's step in one broadcast, rank 0's
keep on its next step, a window's greedy picks in one gather) + 0032
(a step the link refuses leaves rank 0's pending keep for the next
one) (Apache-2.0, (c) MiaAI Lab) against TensorFold v1.2.3
(6ec5fa4cb) + this line's adopted 8-patch stack, 2026-11-07, by this
line - a hand port (0031's hunks carry 0030's moe_fuse plumbing -
the fork stacks them; the port DROPS those bits: no Engine.moe_fuse,
no envOn, no .moe_fuse in the Forward constructions; 0032's
keep-loss guard folded into cuda_follow.zig by hand).

MECHANISM (0031a - the greedy picks): a window's greedy picks ran
one top-1 + one gather + one sync + one device read PER ROW; greedyRows
batches them - one top-1 launch a row, ONE gather of every rank's
words (the pairs buffer is pick_rows=32 rows now), one sync and one
read, each row picked as greedy picks it (chance.pick over the gathered
words, the same tie-breaks). The verify window's rows (DFlash2's
draft length) stop paying a round trip each.

MECHANISM (0031b - the step-link): every step's first broadcast is
384 bytes (the header and up to 80 ids - a decode step's all): one
host round trip on the other ranks instead of two; a longer step's
ids follow in a second broadcast. Rank 0 commits a keep at once and
sends it on its next verify/block/draft step of the same slot
(Link.keep_flag); any other step, or a second keep, sends it alone as
before. A follower's verify and shared steps join their draws'
gathers and skip the sync and read (Engine.discard_draws): rank 0 alone
reads those tokens.

MECHANISM (0032): a step the link refuses (TooManyIds) is refused
WHOLE before a pending keep is sent or put on it, so a refused step can
never lose a keep rank 0 has already committed; glm_pages_host'
hand-built Link sets keep_pending null.

No arithmetic changes: the steps' GPU work runs in the same order on
every rank, and each pick is picked as greedy picked it - the replies
are the same.

PORT NOTES: cuda_engine_pick.zig + cuda_follow.zig - 0031's hunks
apply verbatim (v1.2.3's files match the fork's baseline);
glm_pages_host.zig - 0032's verbatim. cuda_engine.zig - pick_rows
beside pair_bytes, Engine.discard_draws, the pairs buffer pick_rows
wide (alloc + memset), draw()'s discard branch (smp.gather) and the
greedyRows call. cuda_follow.zig - 0032's guard by hand. STAGING:
applies on v1.2.3 + the 8-patch stack (verified byte-identical to the
port commit on a fresh checkout); NAMED glm-zz- TO SORT AFTER THE
STACK (the engine hunks assume the moeside port's side field).
OWNER: this line; STATUS: EXPERIMENTAL, judged by the steplink window
(the content gate + the decode rows, the definitive protocol).

